  * imaginary. Whether they are supported is decided by the renderer's own
  * matrices, computed by the same function that builds the color transform, so
  * acceptance and rendering cannot disagree about supported colorimetry.
+ *
+ * Mastering display primaries are validated the same way. They may lie
+ * outside the primary color volume (extended_target_volume is advertised):
+ * they are kept and take part in identity, but no gamut is mapped with them,
+ * so a target beyond the primary volume cannot cause artifacts. Likewise the
+ * mastering luminance may exceed the primary volume's range; only the smaller
+ * of the two bounds the content.
